1
00:07:24,000 --> 00:07:30,000
The true story of a love that shook an empire

2
00:14:48,000 --> 00:14:54,000
A United Kingdom is a drama, history film directed by Amma Asante.

3
00:22:12,000 --> 00:22:18,000
The inspiring true story of Seretse Khama, the King of Bechuanaland (modern Botswana), and Ruth Williams, the London office worker he
married in 1948 in the face of fierce opposition from their families and the British and South African governments.

4
00:29:36,000 --> 00:29:42,000
Seretse and Ruth defied family, Apartheid and empire - their love triumphed over every obstacle flung
in their path and in so doing they transformed their nation and inspired the world.

5
00:37:00,000 --> 00:37:06,000
Seretse Khama, played by David Oyelowo.

6
00:44:24,000 --> 00:44:30,000
Ruth Williams-Khama, played by Rosamund Pike.

7
00:51:48,000 --> 00:51:54,000
Rufus Lancaster, played by Tom Felton.

8
00:59:12,000 --> 00:59:18,000
Sir Alistair Canning, played by Jack Davenport.

9
01:06:36,000 --> 01:06:42,000
Naledi Khama, played by Terry Pheto.

10
01:14:00,000 --> 01:14:06,000
Muriel Williams, played by Laura Carmichael.

11
01:21:24,000 --> 01:21:30,000
Events from the year 2016 in the United Kingdom.

12
01:28:48,000 --> 01:28:54,000
The year was dominated by the UK's vote to leave the European
Union and the subsequent political fallout.

13
01:36:12,000 --> 01:36:18,000
The film explores themes of based on novel or book, africa,
marriage, biography, based on true story.

14
